  "kind": "excel-differs-from-math",
  "title": "Text to number checks the exponent range even when the mantissa is zero",
  "statement": "Converting text to a number, measured through ABS and VALUE, rejects a zero mantissa with an out-of-range exponent: ABS(\"0e-309\") is #VALUE! though the text denotes 0, and ABS(\"0e-308\") is 0. The exponent counts as written, less the fraction digits, less 2 for a percent sign, so ABS(\"0.0e309\") is 0, ABS(\"0e309\") is #VALUE!, and ABS(\"0e-307%\") is #VALUE!.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "About 120 recorded zero-mantissa cases through ABS, and 72 through VALUE. All 72 VALUE readings fit a limit of -308 to 308 on the exponent as counted here.",
  "inferred": "The exponent formula is inferred, though it fits every reading; that functions other than ABS and VALUE share this conversion is inferred.",
  "documentation": null,
